%% Ask my course (requirement 0006) — the request path and the citation invariant.
%% Derived from ADR 0001 (scope query), ADR 0002 (citations validated against scope),
%% ADR 0007 (one structured request), ADR 0008 (event in the same write), CLAUDE.md.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor L as Learner
  participant W as apps/web
  participant A as apps/api
  participant F as Firestore
  participant G as Gemini (Vertex AI)

  L->>W: a question, and the sessions to ask it against
  W->>A: question + sessionIds — Bearer ID token
  A->>A: resolve the learner  ·  scope = the named sessions this learner owns
  A->>F: materials WHERE session IN (scope) — ADR 0001: a scope query, no index, no similarity search
  F-->>A: one gs:// URI per material, each carrying its session
  A->>A: label every document in the prompt with its session<br/>"Document 3 = Session 5 · Thermodynamics · lecture slides"
  A->>G: one structured request — ADR 0007<br/>documents by gs:// URI, response schema with citations[]
  G-->>A: { answer, citations: [ { sessionId, page } ] }
  A->>A: ADR 0002 — is every cited sessionId in the scope that was sent?
  alt a cited session is outside the scope sent
    A->>G: retry the same request
    G-->>A: new payload
    A->>A: if it recurs — withhold  ·  never show the unverified answer
    A-->>W: nothing shown  ·  the withholding is an event the operator can see (0009)
  else no attributable session
    A-->>W: withheld, for the same reason
  else the material does not cover it
    A-->>W: say so plainly and name what appears missing — never a guess from general knowledge
  else every citation is inside the scope
    A->>F: the event, in the same write — ADR 0008<br/>{ name, occurredAt, learner, requirement: 0006, attributes: { cost, … } }
    A-->>W: answer + citations
    W-->>L: the answer names its session  ·  one click reaches the source material itself
  end
